  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Sec. 732(a)(1), in a current distribution the partner''s basis in distributed property is the lesser of the property''s inside basis ($50,000) or the partner''s outside basis ($80,000). Since $50,000 is less, Partner E takes a $50,000 carryover basis. Unlike a liquidating distribution under Sec. 732(b), a current distribution preserves carryover basis.
Wrong (B): $80,000 is the partner''s outside basis, not the distributed property''s basis; Sec. 732(a) uses the lesser of inside or outside basis.
Wrong (C): $120,000 is FMV, which is irrelevant for basis determination in a current distribution under Sec. 732(a).
Wrong (D): $30,000 has no computational basis under the Sec. 732(a) formula.$EXPL$
