Wrong (B): Distributions do not come first; income must be added before distributions are subtracted to determine whether distributions exceed basis.
Wrong (C): Losses are applied last, not second; the ordering ensures distributions and nondeductible expenses reduce basis before loss limitations are tested.
Wrong (D): Nondeductible expenses come after distributions, not before them, under the statutory ordering rules.$EXPL$
