-- Q4205: Advanced Basis Calculations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 732(b), the partner''s outside basis ($50,000) is allocated across properties in a liquidating distribution. Since total inside basis ($70,000) exceeds outside basis, Sec. 732(c) allocates the decrease proportionally: Property 1 gets $50,000 x ($30,000/$70,000) = $21,429 and Property 2 gets $50,000 x ($40,000/$70,000) = $28,571.
Wrong (A): Equal allocation of $25,000 each ignores Sec. 732(c)''s proportional allocation rules based on relative adjusted basis.
Wrong (B): Keeping Property 1 at inside basis ($30,000) and shortchanging Property 2 ($20,000) does not follow the proportional decrease method.
Wrong (D): This allocation does not follow the Sec. 732(c) proportional formula based on relative adjusted basis of the properties.$EXPL$
