-- Q4206: Advanced Basis Calculations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Sec. 752, when a nonrecourse liability is converted to recourse, the liability must be reallocated based on economic risk of loss under Reg. Sec. 1.752-2. Before conversion, Partner M''s share was $20,000 (one-third of $60,000). After conversion with M bearing all economic risk, M''s share becomes $60,000, a net increase of $40,000 to outside basis.
Wrong (A): $120,000 reflects no change, but the reallocation of the recourse liability to M increases outside basis by M''s net additional share.
Wrong (C): $160,000 overstates the increase by adding the full $60,000 liability rather than the net increase of $40,000 above M''s prior $20,000 share.
Wrong (D): $100,000 incorrectly reduces basis, but a shift to bearing more economic risk increases a partner''s outside basis under Sec. 752(a).$EXPL$
